From 39d61ede6ea20e88968875a0335923a8fde16de8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 05:01:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Coverage from per-sample texture alpha (F-223A)

- hdAlphaAASharp 3: the leaf texture is fetched again at each MSAA sample
  position (explicit gradients, same mip) right after the shader's own
  sample; sample k passes when a * t_k.w / t.w >= ref, written to
  gl_SampleMask with alpha to coverage off (key bit 6, module "#sa<N>")
- Keeps blades thinner than a pixel, which one alpha per pixel cannot;
  modules without a 2D sample in the first block fall back to analytic

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UHcJJVC4feQ4s15e9bNRoN
