      * off. The edge is placed and oriented per sample like the supersampled test, from one shader run per pixel;
      * the alpha output is left as it is.
      *
+     * Zeppelin F-223A, sampleAlpha (hdAlphaAASharp 3, "#sa<N>"): the texture's alpha is read at each sample instead
+     * of extrapolated. The first 2D texture sample of the entry function's first block (the leaf / blade texture) is
+     * fetched again right after it at each sample position (coordinate + its fine derivatives x the sample offset,
+     * explicit gradients so the mip stays the same), and sample k's alpha is a * t_k.w / t.w (the shader's own
+     * alpha, the vertex fade included, rescaled by the texture alone). That keeps blades thinner than a pixel, which
+     * one alpha per pixel cannot -- what the supersampled test gets, without running the whole shader per sample.
+     * A module without such a sample is refused (the build falls back to analytic coverage).
+     *
      * @return uint32 : 1 when patched, 0 when the module is not one this applies to (left unchanged)
